For a real number  $a$ , let  $F_a(x)=\sum_{n\geq 1}n^ae^{2n}x^{n^2}$  for  $0\leq x<1$ . Find a real number  $c$  such that
\begin{align*}
\lim_{x\to 1^-}F_a(x)e^{-1/(1-x)}&=0 \ \ \  \text{for all  $a<c$ , and}
\lim_{x\to 1^-}F_a(x)e^{-1/(1-x)}&=\infty \ \ \  \text{for all  $a>c$ .}
\end{align*}

