It's well known that  $$ \begin{aligned}
&9(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)\ge8(a+b+c)(ab+bc+ca)
\Longrightarrow\;\;&\frac{3}{ab+bc+ca}\ge\frac13\sum_{cyc}\frac4{(a+b)(b+c)}.
\end{aligned} $$  So by applying it to LHS we have  $$ \begin{aligned}
\mathrm{LHS}&\ge n\sum_{i=1}^n\sum_{j=1}^n\sum_{k=1}^n\left(\frac13\sum_{cyc}\frac4{(a_i+a_j)(a_j+a_k)}\right)
&=n\sum_{i=1}^n\sum_{j=1}^n\sum_{k=1}^n\sum_{cyc}\frac4{(a_i+a_j)(a_j+a_k)}
&=n\sum_{i=1}^n\left(\sum_{j=1}^n\frac2{a_i+a_j}\right)\left(\sum_{k=1}^n\frac2{a_i+a_k}\right)
&=n\sum_{i=1}^n\left(\sum_{j=1}^n\frac2{a_i+a_j}\right)^2.
\end{aligned} $$  Let  $\sum\limits_{j=1}^n\dfrac2{a_i+a_j}=x_i$ , by Cauchy-Schwarz we have  $$ \mathrm{LHS}\ge\left(\sum_{i=1}^n x_i\right)^2=\mathrm{RHS}. $$

