\[\angle SFE = \angle SFA_2 = \angle SQA_2 = \angle SQC = \angle SBC\]
Using similar reasoning, we deduce that
\[\angle SEF = \angle SCB\]
so triangles  $\triangle SFE$  and  $\triangle SBC$  are similar, which proves the claim, and thus finishes the proof. \qed

