By power of a point, \begin{align*} \text{ $ABCD$  cyclic} \iff x(x+7) &= y(y+8)  \text{ $PQRS$  cyclic} \iff (x+3)(x+4) &= (y+2)(y+6). \end{align*} However, the latter equation is just the former with  $12$  added to both sides. (That is,  $(x+3)(x+4) = x(x+7)+12$  while  $(y+2)(y+6)=y(y+8)+12$ .) So the conclusion is immediate.
