<span style="color:blue">**Case where  $AB$  and  $CD$  are parallel.**</span> In that case  $ABCD$  is an isosceles trapezoid. Then the entire picture is symmetric around the common perpendicular bisector of the lines  $AB$  and  $CD$ . Now  $PQRS$  is also an isosceles trapezoid, so it's cyclic too.
