<span style="color:#3D85C6">**Claim:**</span>  $f(x^2) = x^2f(x)$ *Proof.* Note that  $P(0, 0)$  gives that  $f(f(0)) = 0$ . Then from  $P(x, 0)$  we find,
\begin{align*}
f(x^2) = f(f(x)) + f(0)
\end{align*}
Additionally, from  $P(x, x^2)$  we find,
\begin{align*}
f(0) + 2x^2f(x) &= f(f(x)) + f(x^2)
\end{align*}
Then setting this equal,
\begin{align*}
x^2f(x) = f(f(x))
\end{align*}
as desired.  $\square$ <span style="color:#c00">**Claim:**</span>  $f(0) = 0$ *Proof.* Consider taking  $P(x, 0)$  and using our prior identity to find,
\begin{align*}
f(x^2) &= f(f(x)) + f(0)
\iff f(x^2) &= f(x^2) + f(0)
\iff f(0) &= 0
\end{align*}
as desired.  $\square$ <span style="color:#3D85C6">**Claim:**</span>  $f$  is even.
*Proof.* Note that from  $P(0, y)$  we find,
