By symmetry, there are  $12$  such moves. Now, consider the middle  $4$  squares of the board. If the king is situated at one of these squares, any subsequent move is not pleasant. Finally, consider the  $8$  squares that border the middle  $4$  squares. If the king is situated at one of these squares, the following move is pleasant if and only if the king goes to one of the middle four squares. Thus, we will have at least  $4$  unpleasant moves of this kind. It is easy to see that none of these overlap, and hence there are at most  $44$  pleasant moves.  $\blacksquare$

