\end{align*}
Now, comparing  $P(x,y), P(x,-y)$  we get   $$ f(x+f(y^2))=f(x)+yf(x+y)-f(xy)=f(x)-yf(x-y)-f(-xy) $$   so,   $$ yf(x+y)+yf(x-y)=f(xy)-f(-xy), $$   here  $x=0$  gives  $f(-y)=-f(y)$ . So  $yf(x+y)+yf(x-y)=2f(xy)$  and swapping  $x,y$  we get   $$ yf(x+y)+yf(x-y)=2f(xy)=xf(x+y)+xf(y-x)=xf(x+y)-xf(x-y) $$   implies  $\frac{f(x+y)}{x+y}=\frac{f(x-y)}{x-y}$  for all  $x\neq \pm y$ . So  $f(x)/x$  is constant. We can check these are the answers.

