We consider complex numbers with  $\odot ABC$  as the unit circle. By  $\textbf{EGMO 6.23.}$ , we have, for some  $u,v,w$ :  $$ a=u^2, b=v^2, c=w^2; p=-uw, q=-uv; i=-uv-uw-vw $$  (here,  $i$  denotes the complex number equal to point  $I$  and  $\textbf{not}$  the number  $\sqrt{-1}$ )  $$ \color{magenta} \bigstar\color{magenta} \boxed{\textbf{Calculations.}}\color{magenta} \bigstar $$  Notice that  $$ \begin{aligned}
& AQRB=\text{paralellogram} \iff 
\iff & a+r=q+b  
\iff & u^2+v^2=-uv+r 
\iff & \boxed{r=u^2+uv+v^2},
\end{aligned} $$  and similarly,  $$ \begin{aligned}
& ASCP=\text{paralellogram} \iff 
\iff & a+c=s+p  
\iff & u^2+w^2=-uw+s 
\iff & \boxed{s=u^2+uw+w^2}.
\end{aligned} $$  All that remains is to prove  $$ \begin{aligned}
\angle IST &= 180^\circ - \angle IRT  \iff 
\iff 180^\circ - \angle ISC &= 180^\circ - \angle IRB 
\angle ISC &= \angle IRB,
\end{aligned} $$  which is equivalent to  $$ \begin{aligned}
\arg \left( \frac{i-s}{c-s}\right)&=\arg \left( \frac{i-r}{b-r}\right)  \iff 
( \text{again, }i \neq \sqrt{-1}; \;& i=-uv-uw-vw ) 
\iff \arg \left( \frac{-uv-vw-uw-u^2-uw-w^2}{w^2-u^2-uw-2^2} \right) &= \arg \left( \frac{-uv-vw-uw-u^2-uv-v^2}{v^2-u^2-uv-v^2} \right)
\iff \arg \left( \frac{u^2+uw+w^2+uw+vw+vu}{u(u+w)} \right) &= \arg \left( \frac{u^2+uv+v^2+uv+vw+uw}{u(u+v)} \right)
\iff \arg \left( \frac{u+v+w}{u} \right) &= \arg \left( \frac{u+w+v}{u} \right),
\end{aligned} $$  which is obviously true. Thus, we are done.</details>

