We magically define  $Q'$  this way:
Define  $Q'$  as the orthogonal projection of  $P$  onto  $Z_1Z_2$ <span style="color:#f00">**Claim:**</span>  $Z_1Z_2\perp AB$  
<span style="color:#f00">**Proof:**</span> From the right triangle  $PDZ_1$  and the fact that  $O_1A=O_1D$ , we have  $$ \frac{PO_1}{PZ_1}=\frac{ \frac{PA+PD}{2} }{PD} = \frac{\frac{PB+PC}{2}}{PC} = \frac{PO_2}{PZ_2}  $$  hence  $Z_1Z_2\parallel O_1O_2$ . Since  $O_1O_2\perp AB$ , the claim is proven

Since  $Q'$  is the orthogonal projection of  $P$  onto  $Z_1Z_2$ , hence  $PQ' \parallel AB $ .

Since  $\measuredangle PQ'Z_1=\measuredangle PQ'Z_2 = 90^\circ$ , pentagons  $PQ'DZ_1Y$  and  $PQ'CZ_2X$  are cyclic.

<span style="color:#f00">**Claim:**</span>  $Q'=Q$  
<span style="color:#f00">**Proof:**</span> We will prove that  $Q'$  lies on  $BY$ . Observe that
    \begin{align*}
        \measuredangle(YB,Q'Y) &= \measuredangle(YB,BA)+\measuredangle(BA,Z_1Q')+\measuredangle(Z_1Q',Q'Y) 
