Here is a fun overkill solution that makes use of [Carnot's Theorem](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnot%27s_theorem_(conics)) :)
------------------------------------------**Solution.** Let  $DP\cap CM=P_1$  and  $DQ\cap EM=Q_1$ . If we can show  $P,Q,P_1,Q_1,K,L$  lie on a conic then the result of the problem follows by Pascal's Theorem. As  $K$  and  $L$  both have equal power with respect to  $(ADB)$  and  $(CME)$  we have that line  $KL$  is the radical axes of these two circles. Since the centers of both of these circles lie on the perpendicular bisector of  $AB$ , we can conclude that  $KL\parallel AB$ .

Clearly triangles  $KDL$ ,  $EDQ_1$ , and  $P_1DC$  are all similar to triangle  $ADB$ . We get that  $P_1,Q_1\in (DLK)$ . Let  $(DLK)$  meet  $CE$  at  $X_1$  and  $X_2$ . Since  $X_1,X_2,L,K,P_1,Q_1$  also lie on a conic, by Carnot's Theorem our desired points lie on a conic if and only if   $$ \frac{|CX_1|\cdot |CX_2|}{|EX_1|\cdot |EX_2|}=\frac{|CP|\cdot |CQ|}{|EP|\cdot |EQ|}. $$   Since  $(CELK)$  is also cyclic we have that  $P_1Q_1\parallel CE$  and hence  $P_1Q_1X_1X_2$  is an isosceles trapezoid. Notice that  $X_1$  and  $X_2$  are isogonal in angle  $\angle CDE$  as  $\angle Q_1DX_2=\angle P_1DX_1$ . The desired ratios now follow from Steiner's Ratio Lemma.
[asy]
import geometry;
size(10cm);
pair M=dir(90);
pair A=(.4,1);
pair B=(-.4,1);
pair C=dir(140);
pair E=dir(30);
pair[] D=intersectionpoints(circle(A,M,E),circle(B,M,C));
pair D=D[0];
pair L=extension(M,C,B,D);
pair K=extension(M,E,A,D);
pair P=extension(C,E,K,K+M-C);
pair Q=extension(C,E,L,L+M-E);
pair N=L+K-M;
pair P_1=extension(D,P,C,M);
pair Q_1=extension(D,Q,E,M);
pair P_2=extension(D,P_1,L,K);
pair Q_2=extension(D,Q_1,L,K);
fill(C--D--E--Q_1--Q_2--P_2--P_1--cycle,white+palegreen);
fill(L--D--P_2--cycle,palegreen);
fill(K--D--Q_2--cycle,palegreen);
draw(circle(A,M,E),darkred);
draw(circle(B,M,C),darkred);
draw(A--B--C--D--E--cycle);
draw(C--M--E--cycle);
draw(L--K);
draw(circle(D,L,K),heavyred+dashed+linewidth(.7));
draw(D--P_1);
draw(D--Q_1);
draw(A--D--B);
draw(L--Q); draw(P--K); draw(M--D,dashed);
draw(conic(P,Q,L,K,P_1),orange+linewidth(.7));
dot(" $A$ ",A,dir(A));
dot(" $B$ ",B,dir(B));
dot(" $C$ ",C,dir(C));
dot(" $D$ ",D,dir(240));
dot(" $E$ ",E,dir(E));
dot(" $P$ ",P,dir(230));
dot(" $Q$ ",Q,dir(-60));
dot(" $P_1$ ",P_1,.6*dir(120));
dot(" $Q_1$ ",Q_1,dir(Q_1));
dot(" $L$ ",L,dir(160));
dot(" $K$ ",K,dir(20));
dot(" $M$ ",M,dir(M));
dot(N);
pair []X=intersectionpoints(circle(D,L,K),line(C,E));
dot(" $X_2$ ",X[0],dir(60));
dot(" $X_1$ ",X[1],.8*dir(120));
[/asy]

