Let  $M$  be the midpoint of major arc  $BC$ . Let  $AF$  and  $DE$  intersect  $(ABCD)$  again at  $P$  and  $Q$  respectively. We will show that  $PFEQ$  is cyclic with circumcenter  $M$ .

First note that  $CDPA$  and  $BAQD$  are isosceles trapezoids. Using arguments of lines, we have
\begin{align*}
&AP+AQ-2AM
=&CD+(AB+DQ-BD)-(AB+AC)
=&CD+(2AB-BD)-(AB+AC)
=&AB+CD-AC-BD
=&0
\end{align*}
Thus,  $AM$  is the angle bisector of  $\angle QAP$ . It follows that  $M$  is an arc midpoint of  $PQ$  and  $|MP|=|MQ|$ ; let  $\omega$  be the circle centered at  $M$  passing through  $P$  and  $Q$ . Since  $|AQ|=|BD|=|AF|$ , we have that  $F$  is the reflection of  $Q$  over  $AM$  and thus lies on  $\omega$ . Similarly,  $E$  lies on  $\omega$ . Now the perpendicular bisectors of  $BC$  and  $EF$  intersect at  $M$  on  $(ABCD)$ .

