Beautiful Problem! We're going to present two solutions.
-----
<span style="color:#008000">**Solution 1 (MMP by my brother *Phoenix*)**</span> 

We will use the Moving Point Method. Move \( R \) along \( \overleftrightarrow{AO} \).  
Note that \( \deg R = 1 \), and since \( \deg E = 0 \), we have \( \deg \overleftrightarrow{ER} \le 1 \).  
Since \( \overleftrightarrow{EP} \) is \( \overleftrightarrow{ER} \) rotated \( 90^\circ \) at fixed point \( E \), we get \( \deg \overleftrightarrow{EP} = \deg \overleftrightarrow{ER} = 1 \), so \( \deg P \le \deg \overleftrightarrow{EP} + \deg \overleftrightarrow{AB} = 1 \).  
Similarly, \( \deg Q \le 1 \), so \( \deg \overleftrightarrow{PQ} \le 2 \).  
Let \( \ell' = \overleftrightarrow{RH} \) rotated by \( 90^\circ \) at fixed point \( H \). Then \( \deg \ell' = \deg \overleftrightarrow{RH} \le 1 \).  
Let \( P_{\infty \ell'} \) be the point at infinity of the line \( \ell' \), i.e. \( P_{\infty \ell'} = \ell' \cap \text{line at infinity} \), so \( \deg P_{\infty \ell'} \le \deg \ell' + 0 = 1 \).  
The condition \( \overleftrightarrow{PQ} \perp \overleftrightarrow{RH} \) is equivalent to points \( P, Q, P_{\infty \ell'} \) being collinear, which is a polynomial condition of degree at most \( \deg P + \deg Q + \deg P_{\infty \ell'} \le 1 + 1 + 1 = 3 \).  
So it suffices to verify 4 values of \( R \).**Case Check:**  
We need to verify the condition \( \overleftrightarrow{PQ} \perp \overleftrightarrow{RH} \) for 4 special positions of \( R \):  
– \( R = A \)  
– \( R = \overleftrightarrow{AO} \cap \overleftrightarrow{BE} \)  
– \( R = \overleftrightarrow{AO} \cap \overleftrightarrow{CF} \)  
– \( R = P_{\infty AO} \) (the point at infinity along \( \overleftrightarrow{AO} \))

