<span style="color:#f00">**<u>Proof</u>**</span>: We already know that \( R, H \) are isogonal conjugates with respect to \( \angle TFA \), \( \angle FAE \), and \( \angle AET \). Thus, the claim follows directly (the proof is just applying the Sine Law). \(\square\)

-----

<span style="color:#00f">**<u>Claim 2</u>**</span>: \( P, Q \) are isogonal with respect to \( \angle FRE \).

<span style="color:#f00">**<u>Proof</u>**</span>: Apply DDIT to \( R \) and cyclic quadrilateral \( PFQE \).  
