Now, we can easily see that \( R, H \) are isogonal conjugates with respect to both \( \triangle AEP \) and \( \triangle AFQ \). Introduce a point \( K \) on line \( PQ \) such that \( HK \perp PQ \).

<span style="color:#00f">**<u>Claim 3</u>**</span>: \( F, E \) are isogonal conjugates with respect to \( \angle PKQ \).

<span style="color:#f00">**<u>Proof</u>**</span>: Note that \( \Box FHKP \) and \( \Box EHKQ \) are concyclic.  
