Let  $T$  be the midpoint of the arc  $EF$  of  $(BEF)$  that does not contain  $B$ .
Since  $H$  and  $B$  lie on opposite sides of line  $AP$ , then  $T$  and  $H$  lie on the same side as line  $AP$ .
Let  $\angle ACD = \alpha$  and  $\angle ADC = \beta$ , where  $90^\circ > \alpha > \beta>0^\circ$ .
Let  $R$  be the radius of the circumcenter of  $(PMN)$  and  $r=MA$  be the radius of  $\Omega$ .

We will use trigonometry to prove that  $HT\parallel AP$ . We will do this by showing  $d(H,AP)=d(T,AP)$  through trigonometric computation.
(We let  $d(X,\ell)$  be the distance from point  $X$  to a line  $\ell$ . )
First, we do a few angle chasing on angles that will be used in later computations:**Some Chasing:**

<span style="color:#f00">**Claim:**</span>  $\Delta BEF \sim \Delta  AMN$ <span style="color:#f00">**Proof:**</span> Observe that
\begin{align*}
\angle BEF &= 180^\circ - \angle BEA = \angle  BMA = 2\angle ACD = 2\alpha 
\angle AMN &= 2\angle ACD = 2\alpha
\end{align*}
So,  $\angle BEF=2\alpha=\angle AMN$  and analogously,  $\angle BFE = 2\beta = \angle ANM$  Claim proven  $\square$ Observe that  $$ \angle BAE = \angle PAC - \angle CAB = \left(90^\circ - \frac{1}{2} \angle CPA\right) - (90^\circ - \angle ACD) = (90^\circ - \beta) - (90^\circ - \alpha) = \alpha - \beta. $$  Since  $AB\perp CD$  and  $PH \perp CD$  imply  $AB\parallel PH$ ,
we have  $\boxed{\angle APH = \angle BAE = \alpha - \beta}$ . $PM\perp AC$  and  $PN\perp AD$  implies  $\angle MPN = 180^\circ - \angle CAD = \alpha + \beta$ . Moreover, by proof of Claim, we have that  $\angle EBF=180^\circ - 2\alpha - 2\beta$ . Since  $TE=TF$ , we have  $\angle TFE = 90^\circ - \frac{1}{2}\angle ETF = \alpha + \beta$ .
Hence,  $\boxed{\angle MPN = \angle TFE = \alpha + \beta}$ .

Now, we are ready to prove  $d(H,AP)=d(T,AP)$ .**Trigonometric Computation:**
Since  $H$  is the orthocenter of  $\Delta PMN$  with circumradius  $R$ , then it is well known that  $HP = 2R \cos(\angle MPN)$ . Hence,
\begin{align*}
d(H,AP) &= HP\cdot \sin(\angle APH)
&= HP\cdot \sin(\alpha - \beta)
&= 2R \cos(\angle MPN)\cdot \sin(\alpha - \beta)
&= 2R \cos(\alpha + \beta) \sin(\alpha - \beta)
\end{align*}And
\begin{align*}
d(T,AP) &= \frac{1}{2}\cdot EF \cdot \frac{\cos(\alpha+\beta)}{\sin(\alpha + \beta)} &= \frac{1}{2}\cdot  \frac{EF}{BE}  \cdot BE \cdot \frac{\cos(\alpha+\beta)}{\sin(\alpha + \beta)}
&= \frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{MN}{MA}  \cdot BE \cdot \frac{\cos(\alpha+\beta)}{\sin(\alpha + \beta)}
