Also, by claim- $2$ ,  $\angle AMN=\angle MNX=\angle NMB$ . So, by symmetry,  $BMNX$  is an isosceles trapezoid as desired.  $\square$ <span style="color:#0B5394">**Claim**</span>:  $H$  is the incentre of  $\triangle MXN$ .
<span style="color:#0B5394">*Proof*</span>: As  $MH \perp NF$  and  $NF \perp AD$ (this is because  $NF$  is the perpendicular bisector of  $AD$ ), we have  $MH ||AD$ .
Then, \[\angle HMN=\angle NDA=\angle NAD=\angle XMH\] which implies  $MH$  bisects  $\angle XMN$ . Similarly,  $NH$  bisects  $\angle MNX$  which implies  $H$  is the incentre of  $\triangle XMN$  as desired.  $\square$ <span style="color:#0B5394">**Claim**</span>:  $BEXF$  is cyclic.
