    where the last equality holds by claim- $3$ . Hence,  $BEXF$  is cyclic as desired.  $\square$ Now, \[\angle HXE=\frac{1}{2}\angle MXN=\frac{1}{2}\angle MAN=\angle MAE=\angle MEA\] which gives  $HX||AP$ . 

Now, we have \[\angle XEF=\angle MEA=\frac{1}{2}\angle MAN=\frac{1}{2}\angle MXN=\angle NXH=\angle XFE\] as  $HX ||AP$ . This gives  $XE=XF$ .

Again, \[\angle HXE=\angle AEM=\angle XEF=\angle XFE\] which implies  $HX$  is tangent to  $(BEF)$ .

Hence, the line through  $H$  parallel to  $AP$  is tangent to the circumcircle of  $\triangle BEF$ .  $\blacksquare$

