We also know that  $|x-b|^2=|m-b|^2\iff x\overline{x}-\dfrac{x}{b}-b\overline{x}+1=1-b-\dfrac{1}{b}+1\implies bx\cdot\dfrac{a+1-x}{a}-b^2\cdot\dfrac{a+1-x}{a}-x=b-b^2-1\implies$  $\implies abx+bx-bx^2-b^2+b^2x-ax=ab-a\implies bx^2+x(a-b-b^2-ab)+ab-a+b^2=0$ .
Since  $x$  and  $m=1$  are the  $2$  roots of this quadratic equation, by Viete we get  $x+1=\dfrac{ab+b^2+b-a}{b}$ Similarly,  $y+1=\dfrac{ac+c^2+c-a}{c}=\dfrac{1+b+ab-ab^2}{b}$  .
So it is left to prove that  $\dfrac{(f+1)(e+1)}{(x+1)(y+1)}\in\mathbb{R}\iff\dfrac{(b+1)^2}{4b}\in \mathbb{R}\iff \dfrac{(b+1)^2}{4b}=\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{1}{b}+1\right)^2}{4\cdot\dfrac{1}{b}}$ , which is true, so we're done.

We color the labyrinth green and yellow in checkerboard fashion, with the corners being green. Note that there are  $(n + 1)^2$  green cells, and  $(2n + 1)^2 - n^2 - (n + 1)^2 = 2n^2 + 2n$  yellow cells. Note that we cannot visit yellow cells in consecutive steps, so to visit all yellow cells, we need at least  $2((2n^2 + 2n) - 1) = 4n^2 + 4n - 2$  steps, where we start at a yellow cell and visit a different yellow cell every two moves. This is possible using the route shown below:
[asy]
import graph;

size(200);

// Define grid size
int n = 7;

for (int x = 0; x < n; ++x) {
    for (int y = 0; y < n; ++y) {
        if ((x + y) % 2 == 0) {
            fill(box((x, y), (x+1, y+1)), green);
        } else {
            fill(box((x, y), (x+1, y+1)), yellow);
        }
    }
}

// Draw the black squares (preserved from the original image)
pair[] black_squares = {
    (1,5), (3,5), (5,5),
    (1,3), (3,3), (5,3),
    (1,1), (3,1), (5,1)
};

for (pair p : black_squares) {
    fill(box(p, p + (1,1)), black);
}

// Draw the grid
for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {
    draw((i,0)--(i,n), black);
    draw((0,i)--(n,i), black);
}

draw((0.5,1.5)--(0.5,0.5)--(2.4,0.5)--(2.4,1.5)--(2.6,1.5)--(2.6,0.5)--(4.4,0.5)--(4.4,1.5)--(4.6,1.5)--(4.6,0.5)--(6.6,0.5)--(6.6,3.5)--(6.4,3.5)--(6.4,2.5)--(4.6,2.5)--(4.6,3.5)--(4.4,3.5)--(4.4,2.5)--(2.6,2.5)--(2.6,3.5)--(2.4,3.5)--(2.4,2.5)--(0.5,2.5)--(0.5,4.5)--(2.4,4.5)--(2.4,5.5)--(2.6,5.5)--(2.6,4.5)--(4.4,4.5)--(4.4,5.5)--(4.6,5.5)--(4.6,4.5)--(6.5,4.5)--(6.5,6.5)--(0.5,6.5)--(0.5,5.5), red+dashed);

[/asy]
Hence, the answer is  $\boxed{4n^2 + 4n - 2}$ .  $\Box$

